Emma Bauer started crying. Thor, her stocky teenage brother, went over and put his arms around her.

Helen, Emma's mother, looked straight into Gary's eyes and started slow clapping. Thor took off his baseball cap and used the bill to wipe his own eyes. He put his thumb to his mouth and blew noisily.

Gary looked angry, then triumphant, as though he'd known all along they would react that way. He reclosed his notebook and didn't look at Joan. Joan followed Gary outside. "I'm sorry, Gary. Are you sure that's the right thing to do?" Gary said, "I don't need company. It's what the rules say."

Joan stepped into the stream of cars exiting the lot. Most had their music too loud. She walked home, knowing she probably wouldn't get much sleep that night. Emma had gotten that ramp because she'd been brave enough to say no to a kid in a car. She'd gotten it because not everyone in that car had been a bully. She hadn't gotten that ramp because the Bauers or their neighbors were rich or famous. She'd gotten it the way this town was supposed to work. She'd told the world that the ramp was part of what made a sidewalk a good sidewalk. That afternoon the Bauers bowed to the HOA's decision. The next day both families moved. Question: What is most likely to be true about Joan? === The answer to the above question is

OPTIONS:
 *She has OCD;
 *She likes law and order;
 *not enough information;
 *She likes rules alot, but will break them if necessary;
Answer: She likes law and order
